{"changes":["eka-core/conformance/artifact.go: `ValidUntil` and `LastConfirmed` on Artifact next to Created/Updated; both added to allowedJSONTopLevel AND to the JSON adapter's frontmatter forwarding list (allowlisting without forwarding left them never classified — a gap in the design document, caught during implementation); the date-validation loop generalised so both new dates produce the same RuleStructural finding as `created`.","eka-core/exchange/model.go, builder.go, artifact.go: the two fields on Unit (omitempty, after CaptureMeta, declaration order preserved) and carried both directions through toUnit/ToArtifact.","eka-core/machine/document.go: Document carries both fields with omitempty; `Freshness *Freshness` appended at the very end of the struct after Timeline, so it stays absent until a flag asks for it and the default document remains byte-identical. NewDocument maps the fields and never sets Freshness.","eka-core/runtime/freshness.go (new): FreshnessFor(u, now) is pure — the clock is a parameter and the wall clock is never read, so the same inputs always produce the same verdict. Zero `now` or an absent horizon yields `undeclared`, the honest third state; a horizon yields whole calendar days and current/stale.","eka-core/runtime/draft.go: the fields round-trip through the draft frontmatter and the inlined CKO.","eka-cli/cmd/get.go: `--freshness` on the identity and domain forms; containers query refuses it with exit 2 rather than silently ignoring it.","eka-cli/cmd/status.go: a `Stale knowledge: N (of M bounded)` line and a `freshness` object in --json, reusing the existing unit scan rather than adding a second pass.","eka-standard/specification/exchange.md + rules/rule-001.md: the normative envelope prose and one requirement bullet, with rationale deferred to the ADR. No version bump — an additive optional field is not a corpus release.","eka-cli/go.mod: eka-core v1.10.5 -\u003e v1.10.6 after releasing the new API; README's pinned core version updated to match (the Wave 2 drift test caught the omission, which is the test doing its job)."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Landed the validity horizon for knowledge freshness: two optional dated envelope fields, an advisory-only verdict function with an injected clock, and one query surface on the existing retrieval path plus status.","tests":["eka-core conformance/freshness_test.go (4 tests): a JSON artifact carrying validUntil does not produce an R0 unknown-field error, a malformed date produces a structural finding, and the fields are actually classified rather than merely allowlisted.","eka-core exchange/artifact_roundtrip_test.go: validUntil and lastConfirmed survive artifact -\u003e Unit -\u003e artifact.","eka-core machine/freshness_test.go (5 tests): NewDocument never sets Freshness, and a document without the new fields marshals byte-identically to the pre-change schema.","eka-core runtime/freshness_test.go: a 7-case table covering undeclared (no horizon), undeclared (zero clock), current with days remaining, stale with days past, and an unparseable date; plus nil-unit handling.","eka-cli cmd/get_freshness_test.go (3 tests): the flag adds the block, names the status, and the absent flag leaves output unchanged.","Byte-identical default proof: baseline and new binaries compared against the real workspace on identity, a 380 KB domain query, compact form, and the containers query — all cmp-identical.","eka-core go test ./... -count=1 -\u003e all packages ok (conformance 0.13s, exchange 0.35s, machine 0.01s, runtime 221s, store 164s, sync, view, workspace, contexts).","eka-cli go test ./... -short -count=1 -\u003e all ok (cmd 453s). go build ./... , go vet ./... , gofmt -l . -\u003e clean, with eka-core v1.10.6 required rather than replaced locally.","Manual: `eka get eka/adr:freshness-validity-horizon --freshness` reports status undeclared; `eka status` reports `Stale knowledge: 0 (of 759 bounded)` and `--json` carries {stale: 0, scanned: 759}."]}